{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dynamic difficulty adjustment dynamic difficulty adjustment","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment.md","fileName":"Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 15:28\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Challenge Design]] · [[Game Balance and Difficulty]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Challenge Design","Game Balance and Difficulty","Flow","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dynamic difficulty adjustment dynamic difficulty adjustment","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment.md","fileName":"Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment","heading":"Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Dynamic difficulty adjustment changes rules or resources in response to the player's performance. It may provide more help when the player struggles or increase resistance when the player succeeds, with the aim of keeping the experience near a desired [[Flow|flow state]].\n\nSubtle adjustment can prevent prolonged boredom or frustration. Strong adjustment can make the system feel unstable or \"mushy,\" because the apparent structure changes whenever the player pushes against it and mastery becomes harder to evaluate.\n\nDynamic adjustment can respond to differences in native talent, prior experience, and current performance without requiring the player to select a fixed difficulty mode. It also requires substantial testing, and familiar selectable modes may remain useful when the team cannot build a trustworthy adaptive system.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Challenge Design","Game Balance and Difficulty","Flow","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dynamic difficulty adjustment dynamic difficulty adjustment","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment.md","fileName":"Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Dynamic Difficulty Adjustment","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[agamedesignvocabulary.pdf]]\n\n[[fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Challenge Design","Game Balance and Difficulty","Flow","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}